.TH MINSEC-ID.TOML 5 "2026-10-26" "minsec-id" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
minsec-id.toml \- minsec-id configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/minsec-id/minsec-id.toml
.br
.I /etc/minsec-id/conf.d/*.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minsec-id
reads
.I minsec-id.toml
and then merges every
.I conf.d/*.toml
drop-in over it in name order: tables merge key by key, other values replace
earlier ones.
A missing main file means defaults.
Unknown keys are errors;
.B minsec-id check
validates the result.
.PP
.BR "minsec-id enable" ,
.BR disable ,
and
.B accept
write drop-ins
.RI ( conf.d/ check .toml
and
.IR conf.d/accept.toml ).
.SH DURATIONS
Durations are strings such as
.BR 30s ,
.BR 10m ,
.BR 1h30m ,
.BR 2d ,
or
.BR 1w ,
or a number of seconds.
.SH OUTPUT TABLE
.TP
.BR journal " (boolean, default " true )
Send new and resolved findings to journald.
.TP
.BR exec " (string)"
A command run with
.B /bin/sh \-c
once per new finding, with the finding as JSON on standard input and
.BR MINSEC_CHECK ,
.BR MINSEC_SEVERITY ,
.BR MINSEC_SUBJECT ,
.BR MINSEC_FINGERPRINT ,
and
.B MINSEC_MESSAGE
in the environment.
It is killed after 30 seconds and runs inside the scan service's sandbox.
.TP
.BR min_severity " (default " low )
Notify (journal and
.BR exec )
only at or above this severity:
.BR info ,
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.BR high ,
or
.BR critical .
Everything is still written to the findings log.
.SH SCAN TABLE
.TP
.BR sample_days " (integer, default " 7 )
Full scans re-hash every packaged file over this many days, one slice a day,
in addition to files with evidence of change.
.TP
.BR ctime_slack " (duration, default " 1h )
A packaged file whose ctime is this much newer than its package's install
time has changed since install and is hashed.
.SH PATHS TABLE
.TP
.BR state_dir " (default " /var/lib/minsec-id )
Where state, the findings log, and the verified-file cache live.
.TP
.BR socket " (default " /run/minsec-id/minsec-id.sock )
Reserved for the optional daemon.
.SH CHECKS TABLES
.TP
.B [checks.\fIid\fB]
.RS
.TP
.BR enabled " (boolean)"
Override the check's default.
.TP
.BR severity
Replace the severity of every finding the check emits.
.RE
.SH ACCEPT TABLES
.TP
.B [accept."\fIcheck\fB:\fIsubject\fB"]
Accept findings with this id and subject; a subject ending in
.B *
matches by prefix.
.RS
.TP
.BR reason " (string)"
Why, for whoever reads the file next.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[output]
min_severity = "medium"
exec = "/usr/local/bin/page-oncall"

[scan]
sample_days = 14

[checks.ftrace-hooks]
enabled = false

[accept."kernel-tainted:P"]
reason = "NVIDIA driver"

[accept."exe-unowned:/usr/bin/vendor-*"]
reason = "installed by the vendor's tarball"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minsec-id (1)
